{
  "borough": "Harrow",
  "application_type": "Householder",
  "decision": "Refused",
  "decision_conditions": [
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:18.0pt&quot;&gt;The applicant has failed to\r\ndemonstrate that the existing hardstanding does&amp;nbsp;not exacerbate the risk of\r\nflooding and surface water run-off within the site or increase the risk and\r\nconsequences of flooding elsewhere, contrary to Policy SI13 of The London Plan (2021), Core Policy CS1.U of\r\nHarrow Core Strategy (2012) and Policy DM10 of the Harrow Development\r\nManagement Polices Local Plan (2013).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p class=&quot;MsoNormal&quot; style=&quot;margin-left:18.0pt&quot;&gt;The existing hardstanding and\r\nforecourt treatment, due to its inappropriate materials and the complete loss\r\nof soft landscaping on the front forecourt and side garden, results&amp;nbsp;in a\r\nstark and harsh development out of keeping with the character and appearance of\r\nthe dwelling and the local area, which results in harm to the streetscene, and which is exacerbated by its prominent corner plot location. The development therefore fails to respect the character of the surrounding area and streetscene.\r\nThe proposal therefore fails to comply with National Planning Policy Framework\r\n(2024), Policies D3.D (1) and (11) of the London Plan (2021), Core Policy CS1.B\r\nof the Harrow Core Strategy (2012), policies DM1, DM22.B and DM23 of the Harrow\r\nDevelopment Management Policies Local Plan (2013), the adopted Supplementary\r\nPlanning Document: Residential Design Guide (2010).&lt;o:p&gt;&lt;/o:p&gt;&lt;/p&gt;",
    "&lt;p&gt;&lt;span pt=&quot;&quot; sans=&quot;&quot;&gt;The proposed boundary fence, given its height and location, would have a detrimental impact on highway safety for pedestrians and road users, contrary to&amp;nbsp;Policies DM1.B(g) and&amp;nbsp;DM42.F of the Harrow Development Management Polices Local Plan (2013).&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/p&gt;"
  ],
